### The Wusheng Laomu dimension

This is the analysis's most theoretically complex element. In Xiantiandao:

```
WUSHENG LAOMU (無生老母) — Eternal Venerable Mother
  Supreme female creator deity and salvationist figure.
  The doctrinal center of Xiantiandao.
  She calls humanity back to its primordial home
  from which souls were exiled.
  Her image may or may not be physically present in
  a given zhaitang — some institutions keep her image
  in an inner sanctum visible only to initiates; others
  allow her to be represented symbolically through
  Guanyin佛祖.

GUANYIN's RELATIONSHIP TO WUSHENG LAOMU:
  In Xiantiandao, Guanyin can function as:
    a) A distinct Buddhist bodhisattva venerated
       within a syncretic framework
    b) A manifestation of Wusheng Laomu in accessible
       devotional form
    c) Both simultaneously — the surface form (Guanyin)
       accessible to all, the deeper identity (Wusheng
       Laomu) accessible to initiates

  RFIG documents this as a provisional substitutes
  relation that may be operating at a doctrinal depth
  not fully accessible from iconographic observation alone:

  [GUANYIN  substitutes  WUSHENG_LAOMU]
    [scope: shrine, provisional]
  -- Guanyin may serve as the publicly accessible
     figure of the supreme female deity within
     Xiantiandao's layered disclosure strategy

  This requires institutional confirmation, as the
  degree to which Guanyin佛祖 and Wusheng Laomu are
  identified varies across Xiantiandao communities.
```

